 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by incorrectly serializing `is_overdue` as a string in the `task_to_dict` function. The fix removed the `str()` and `.lower()` conversions, ensuring `is_overdue` is returned as a boolean value. This change passes both the reproduction test and the full test suite.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/serializers.py b/tracker/serializers.py\nindex 986d296..3170695 100644\n--- a/tracker/serializers.py\n+++ b/tracker/serializers.py\n@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@ def user_to_dict(user, include_email=False):\n         data[\"email\"] = user.email\n     return data\n \n-\n def task_to_dict(task, now):\n     return {\n         \"id\": task.id,\n@@ -33,7 +32,7 @@ def task_to_dict(task, now):\n         \"owner_id\": task.owner_id,\n         \"assignee_id\": task.assignee_id,\n         \"due_at\": task.due_at,\n-        \"is_overdue\": str(is_overdue(task.due_at, task.status, now)).lower(),\n+        \"is_overdue\": is_overdue(task.due_at, task.status, now),\n         \"tags\": list(task.tags),\n         \"created_at\": task.created_at,\n         \"updated_at\": task.updated_at,\n",
